Now I have sufficient information to write my verdict. Let me synthesize my findings.

**Summary of verification:**
- arXiv 2504.04372 (ICST 2026, 78% failure rate): ✅ confirmed, correctly described
- arXiv 2505.10443 (nine LLMs, up to 70% drops): ✅ confirmed — paper does evaluate nine LLMs, contrary to one search summary that said six
- arXiv 2601.18044 (RGFL, 85% Hit@1 on SWE-bench Verified): ✅ confirmed
- arXiv 2602.11411 (perturbed SFT, character/word/sentence level, no contrastive loss): ✅ confirmed — differentiation from SeMutFL is accurate
- arXiv 2503.23448 (59% failure rate for published SPTs): ✅ confirmed
- MACL-IRFL (Automated Software Engineering 2026): ✅ confirmed, graph-based not LLM fine-tuning
- EMNLP 2026 ARR deadline May 25, 2026: ✅ confirmed
- 4-ablation worst-case budget (171 H100-hours): ✅ within 200 H100-hour limit
- Qwen2.5-Coder-32B QLoRA training time (22h/run on 2×A100): still loosely grounded — search found 2–12h for single A100 on smaller models; 22h for 32B on 2×A100 is plausible but not directly cited
- Competitive work search: no paper combining InfoNCE contrastive training + semantic code mutations for fault localization LLM fine-tuning was found

