  "scores": {
    "novelty": {
      "score": 4,
      "rationale": "The combination of semantic-preserving code mutations and InfoNCE contrastive fine-tuning for fault localization in LLMs is confirmed novel — no existing paper does this. Differentiation from the closest competitor (arXiv 2602.11411, NLP-level perturbations + plain SFT, code generation tasks) is accurate and clearly articulated. Score stops short of 5 because this is an application of the established ContraCode augmentation paradigm to a new task rather than a fundamentally new training mechanism."
